# ── Private docs (explicitly kept out of the repo) ──────────────────────────
# CLAUDE.md is intentionally SHIPPED (the design + grounding contract); the two below stay local.
HACKATHON_STRATEGY.md
DEMO.md
# Demo / verification runners — kept local for recording, not shipped
scripts/demo_grounding_veto.py
scripts/demo_second_opinion.py

# ── Large input data (exceeds GitHub's 100 MB/file limit — never commit) ─────
# Raw Xenium inputs (~1.4 GB, incl. transcripts.csv.gz 1.3 GB)
Raw_data_Xenium_hbreast_sample1/
# The Zenodo handover (4.3 GB): both samples' vendor bundles plus the processed
# Seurat object. Same rule as the line above, and §12's "fetch
# restrictively-licensed data, never bundle it" -- the bundle is fetched, never
# committed. Panoscope reads it only through the prep step.
data/xenium_human_breast_cancer/
# jazzPanda outputs live here; xenium_hbreast_seu.Rds alone is 328 MB.
# Whole dir ignored for now — small precomputed outputs get committed under
# data/jazzpanda/ once the repo layout is set up.
jazzPanda output/

# SpatialData stores. ARCHITECTURE §5.1 makes the .zarr the on-disk format and
# §12 says fetch restrictively-licensed data, never bundle it -- the human breast
# store is 609 MB, well past GitHub's limit. A study tree carries the store only
# on the machine that built it; a fresh clone draws from the committed
# viz/hexbin/ frames instead (ui/data_access.hexbins prefers the store, falls
# back to the frames). Unignored, this would also break the two journey checks
# that assert `git status --porcelain data/studies/` is empty.
data/studies/*/spatial.zarr/

# Defensive: never let big bio-data blobs in even if relocated
*.csv.gz
*.mtx.gz
*.h5
*.h5ad
xenium_hbreast_seu.Rds

# Fat raw expression matrix (280 genes × all cells, ~55 MB); the committed
# artifact is the subsampled data/embeddings/marker_expr.parquet.
data/embeddings/marker_expr.csv

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ── Secrets / environment ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

